// The executable's icon: the app's mark in the default look (Carbon, dark), as Explorer, the taskbar
// before the window has made its own, and Alt-Tab show it. The file is assets/icon/vibin.ico, made by
//   output/main --write-icon assets/icon/vibin.ico
// from the same drawing as the loading screen (src/daw/AppIcon.cpp); once running, the window's icon
// follows the user's theme (DawApp::refreshWindowIcon).
//
// CMake fills in the path (configure_file) and compiles this with windres.
//
// Explorer shows the icon group with the lowest id (1); GLFW gives its windows' class the one named
// GLFW_ICON, so a window has it from the moment it exists. Both are the same file.
1 ICON "@VIBIN_ICON_FILE@"
GLFW_ICON ICON "@VIBIN_ICON_FILE@"
